                  </h2>

                  <p>
                    ONE+ is the widest homeowner battery platform available, and the mistakes are about how people buy into it rather than about the tools themselves.
                  </p>

                  <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
                      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying Kitted Versions You Do Not Need</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                        Every kitted tool bundles a battery and charger at a substantial premium. Once you own two or three good packs, buy tool-only and put the difference toward another tool. This is the single biggest saving available on the platform.
                      </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
                      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Staying on Compact Batteries</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                        The small packs included in starter kits throttle the high-draw tools badly — circular saws, trimmers, and mowers all sag or cut out on them. One high-capacity high-performance battery transforms how those tools behave and is usually the best upgrade you can make.
                      </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
                      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the Brushed and Brushless Split</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                        Ryobi sells both versions of many tools, and the gap in power, runtime, and motor life is significant. On tools you reach for weekly, the brushless version earns its premium comfortably. On a tool you use twice a year, it does not.
                      </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
                      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting Professional-Duty Performance</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                        ONE+ is built and priced for homeowners and light trade work and is excellent at that. Used all day every day on a site, the tools wear faster than professional lines. Match the platform to the workload rather than expecting it to be something it never claimed to be.
                      </p>
